  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food safety systems and trade facilitation across agri-food value chains in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; background-color: white;&quot;&gt;The proposed project is part of an EU-INTPA regional programme called &#xbf;Alliance for the Horn of Africa Initiative&#xbf;. In this framework, UNIDO has been offered the opportunity to design a project proposal set to strengthening Somalia overall capacities of quality control and standards institutions for inspections, metrology, testing, and certification of priority food products (through standards development, laboratories, equipment, staff training, etc.), including certification of origin, as well as improve collaboration among quality control, standards and certification institutions and with relevant Somali public institutions (e.g. customs, port/airport authorities, police, statistics, Ministries of Commerce and Industry, Agriculture and Fisheries) and private sector. The collaboration set to be put forward by the proposed project, will also include outreach, engagements and partnership facilitation with international standards bodies and institutions from other countries in particular Kenya, Ethiopia and UAE. This will have the very specific objective to move towards the overall international recognition of Somali standards, certification system and its alignment with international best practices. Ultimately, this will in turn, help increase the international recognition of Somali products, starting from selected food products that the proposed project will be directly supporting as part of this intervention.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
